/-!
# Height-one localizations of regular local rings are DVRs (P2.3 prefix)

## Route decision (P2.3) — SUPERSEDED 2026-07-27

This file originally recorded **route (h) homological** (Matsumura §19, Bruns–Herzog 2.2:
regular ⇒ finite global dimension ⇒ localizations regular by Serre ⇒ dim-1 regular = DVR),
following the planning default of `docs/CONSTRUCTION_SELF_BUILD_BRICKS.md` §P2.3.

**That route was not needed.**  P2.3 is closed in
`RiemannRoch/Chow/RegularLocalHeightOnePrincipal.lean` by **route (e), an elementary
dimension-two argument**: the maximal ideal of a two-dimensional regular local ring is
generated by a two-term regular sequence `(a, b)` whose first member can be chosen outside a
given height-one prime `p`; the Koszul syzygy then makes `m ⊗ p → p` injective, so `p` is free
and therefore principal.  No global dimension, no Auslander–Buchsbaum, no `Tor` balancing and
no depth theory is used — see that file for the full route note and the argument that it
avoids both circularity traps below.

### Circularity traps (do not use)
* "`R` normal ⇒ DVR via `TFAE`" presupposes Serre's condition `(R₁)`, which **is** this brick.
* "Nagata with `R[1/x]` a PID" presupposes control of the same height-one localizations.

### What this file lands
1. Dim-1 regular local domain ⇒ DVR (the terminal step, via cotangent finrank + TFAE).
2. Localization at a height-one prime has Krull dimension 1 (dimension bookkeeping).
3. Hence: a *regular* height-one localization of a domain is a DVR.  Regularity of that
   localization is supplied by `RegularLocalHeightOnePrincipal.lean`, so 1–3 together are the
   terminal steps of the closed brick rather than a conditional prefix.
4. Projective dimension of the free module `R` is zero — retained as the free-module seed of
   the plate-P3 Auslander–Buchsbaum formula `pd M + depth M = depth R`, which P2.3 no longer
   depends on.
-/

noncomputable section

universe u

open IsLocalRing ModuleCat CategoryTheory

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

namespace IsRegularLocalRing

/-- A one-dimensional regular local domain is a DVR.

This is the terminal implication of route (h): once a height-one localization is known to be
regular of dimension one, `IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE` / the cotangent criterion finishes.-/
theorem isDiscreteValuationRing_of_ringKrullDim_eq_one
    [IsDomain R] [IsRegularLocalRing R] (hdim : ringKrullDim R = 1) :
    IsDiscreteValuationRing R := by
  have hfin : Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R) = 1 := by
    have hcot :
        Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (CotangentSpace R) = ringKrullDim R :=
      (iff_finrank_cotangentSpace (R := R)).mp inferInstance
    rw [hdim] at hcot
    exact_mod_cast hcot
  exact IsLocalRing.finrank_CotangentSpace_eq_one_iff.mp hfin

/-- Localizing at a height-one prime yields a one-dimensional local ring.-/
theorem ringKrullDim_localizationAtPrime_eq_one_of_height_eq_one
    (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (hp : p.height = 1) :
    ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime p) = 1 := by
  rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height p (Localization.AtPrime p), hp]
  simp

/-- Route-(h) conditional finish: if a height-one localization of a domain is already regular,
then it is a DVR.

The missing plate input is regularity of `Localization.AtPrime p` for regular local `R`
(finite global dimension + Serre), which is shared with plate P3.-/
theorem isDiscreteValuationRing_localizationAtPrime_of_height_one_of_regular
    [IsDomain R] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (hp : p.height = 1)
    [IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime p)] :
    IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p) :=
  isDiscreteValuationRing_of_ringKrullDim_eq_one
    (ringKrullDim_localizationAtPrime_eq_one_of_height_eq_one p hp)

end IsRegularLocalRing

namespace ModuleCat

/-- The free module `R` has projective dimension zero.

Together with the depth API of `RiemannRoch.Chow.Depth`, this is the free-module seed of the
route-(h) / P3 Auslander–Buchsbaum formula `pd M + depth M = depth R` (here `pd R = 0`, so the
identity reduces to `depth R = depth R`).-/
theorem projectiveDimension_self_eq_zero [Small.{u} R] [Nontrivial R] :
    projectiveDimension (ModuleCat.of R R) = 0 := by
  haveI : Projective (ModuleCat.of R R) :=
    (IsProjective.iff_projective (R := R) R).mp inferInstance
  exact projectiveDimension_eq_zero_of_projective _

end ModuleCat
